{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall not say, 'I…'</b> And it is difficult: how can it be justified to say that he made me rich, etc. — is not the Master, YHWH of Hosts, the shield of His beloved?" "<b>Indeed,</b> according to what we explained in the words of the king of Sodom, that he thinks the possessions belong to him, only that he is willing to give him the property, as he said ״הָרְכוּשׁ קַח לָךְ״ — therefore he said that the king of Sodom is acting according to his own understanding, for he thinks the property is his, so that he will not be able to fill his mouth to say ״I made Abram rich; I lifted up… if…״ And in this: ״you shall not say…״ — for in truth, according to the law, they are my possessions which Elohim gave me, and therefore I gave a tithe of everything, as we demonstrated in the commentary on (Genesis 14:21) ״תֶּן לִי הַנֶּפֶשׁ״ etc. And from this it is precisely understood why the verse says <b>וְלֹא תֹאמַר</b> — for he should have said ״וְלֹא אֶתְעַשֵּׁר מִשֶּׁלְּךָ״ ('and I shall not be enriched from what is yours'). Understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:19.098318130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}